.TH QUADRF.CONF 5 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf.conf \- site configuration for a QuadRF appliance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/quadrf/quadrf.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
Plain shell assignments, read by the maintainer scripts of the quadrf-*
packages, by the runtime helpers under
.I /usr/lib/quadrf
and by
.BR quadrf (1).
Nothing else may appear in the file: it is sourced, not parsed.
.PP
Run
.B quadrf apply
after editing. Settings that change the firmware configuration also need a
reboot, which
.B quadrf status
will report.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.B QUADRF_USER
Account that owns the desktop session, the web control panel and the demo
applications. The packages ship generic systemd units and override the user
through a drop-in, so changing this and running
.B quadrf apply
moves the services to another account. Default:
.BR dietpi .
.TP
.B QUADRF_BOOT_DIR
Firmware partition holding
.IR config.txt ,
.I cmdline.txt
and the
.I overlays/
directory. Default:
.IR /boot/firmware .
.TP
.B QUADRF_TLS_DOMAIN
Name on the certificate nginx serves, and the name dnsmasq publishes on the
station interface. Default:
.BR my.quadrf.com .
.TP
.B QUADRF_AP_SSID
SSID of the fallback access point. Default:
.BR QuadRF .
.TP
.B QUADRF_AP_ADDRESS
Address the appliance takes on wlan0 in access point mode, and the target of
the captive DNS wildcard. A /24 is assumed. Default:
.BR 192.168.44.1 .
.TP
.B QUADRF_OPENOCD
OpenOCD binary used to program the FPGA. When empty the first of
.I /usr/lib/quadrf/openocd/bin/openocd
or
.I /usr/bin/openocd
is used.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
QUADRF_USER=operator
QUADRF_BOOT_DIR=/boot/firmware
QUADRF_TLS_DOMAIN=unit14.example.net
QUADRF_AP_SSID=QuadRF-14
QUADRF_AP_ADDRESS=192.168.44.1
QUADRF_OPENOCD=
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf (1)
